  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multi-profile RNA (config_002, acc=0.591) substantially outperforms single-profile RNA (config_001, acc=0.485), and that adding ResNet50 image to single-profile RNA gives a modest gain (config_016, acc=0.527 vs 0.485). The key open question is whether these two gains—multi-profile aggregation and image fusion—are additive or sub-additive. Config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) directly extends our best result (config_002) by adding the image modality while keeping the same RNA encoder and aggregation, allowing a clean comparison: config_018 vs config_002 isolates the image contribution given multi-profile, and config_018 vs config_016 isolates the multi-profile contribution given image. This is the highest-information next step because it tests the most promising direction (our best config + the one other modality that showed positive contribution) with only one new variable changed, and the answer will determine whether further budget should go toward improving the image side (ViT-L, transformer aggregation) or the RNA side (scVI, scGPT encoders)."
}

